{
  "_source": "Worked out by hand from the same rule as money_parse.json (NumberParser in STMCore, parseNumber in Money.kt), for the decimal fields: Decimal(parsing:maxFractionDigits:) and parseDecimal. maxFractionDigits is the field's limit: 8 for a quantity of shares, 6 for a price per share, 3 for a fee rate, 2 for a card rate or an expected return. A single point followed by exactly 3 digits groups thousands only when maxFractionDigits is below 3; with 3 or more it is invalid (1.234 could be 1,234 or 1234). On top of the rule these fields drop a '%' and reject negative numbers. value is the exact decimal in plain notation with a point; null means invalid. Compare numerically (1250 equals 1250.0).",
